IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ddtr-dates`
IMPORT `ddtr-process`
IMPORT `ddtr-fees`
IMPORT `ddtr-offers`

-- Dust Diseases Tribunal Regulation 2019 (NSW) -- cases for every exported question, from the claimant's seat. Every
-- expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text, counting business days on a calendar (1 February 2027 is
-- a Monday; 22 December 2026 is a Tuesday), never copied from the encoding's output.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website at 10 March 2025, via the Open Australian
-- Legal Corpus (version as at 1 July 2022). State of New South Wales, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE
-- ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases`

-- Short names for the cases.
`meso` MEANS `mesothelioma or asbestos-induced carcinoma, with or without another condition`
`asbestosis` MEANS `asbestosis or an asbestos-related pleural disease, and neither mesothelioma nor asbestos-induced carcinoma`
`silicosis` MEANS `a dust-related condition that is not asbestos-related`
`no dust` MEANS `a condition that is not dust-related`
`sufferer` MEANS `the person who is or was suffering from the condition`
`through` MEANS `a person claiming through them, including a compensation to relatives claim`
`1 Feb 2027` MEANS `the regulation date` 1 2 2027

§§ `The business-day arithmetic (cl 11(1), (2)) and rounding (Sch 1 Part 2 cl 3)`

-- Friday 6 November 2026 + 5 business days = Friday 13 November (Mon 9 .. Fri 13).
#ASSERT `the end of` 5 `business days after` (`the regulation date` 6 11 2026) `ignoring Christmas` TRUE EQUALS `the regulation date` 13 11 2026
-- Tuesday 22 December 2026 + 5, ignoring 25 Dec - 9 Jan: Wed 23 (1), Thu 24 (2), Mon 11 Jan (3), Tue 12 (4), Wed 13 (5).
#ASSERT `the end of` 5 `business days after` (`the regulation date` 22 12 2026) `ignoring Christmas` TRUE EQUALS `the regulation date` 13 1 2027
-- The same, counting the Christmas period (weekends still skipped): 23, 24, 25, 28, 29 December.
#ASSERT `the end of` 5 `business days after` (`the regulation date` 22 12 2026) `ignoring Christmas` FALSE EQUALS `the regulation date` 29 12 2026
-- 2 business days before Monday 9 November 2026: Fri 6 (1), Thu 5 (2).
#ASSERT `the latest day` 2 `business days before` (`the regulation date` 9 11 2026) `ignoring Christmas` TRUE EQUALS `the regulation date` 5 11 2026
-- After Friday 6 November up to Friday 13 November: 5; up to Sunday 15 November: still 5; the same day: 0.
#ASSERT `the business days after` (`the regulation date` 6 11 2026) `up to` (`the regulation date` 13 11 2026) `ignoring Christmas` TRUE EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the business days after` (`the regulation date` 6 11 2026) `up to` (`the regulation date` 15 11 2026) `ignoring Christmas` TRUE EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the business days after` (`the regulation date` 6 11 2026) `up to` (`the regulation date` 6 11 2026) `ignoring Christmas` TRUE EQUALS 0
-- 50 cents is rounded down; 51 cents up; 49 cents down.
#ASSERT `rounded to the nearest dollar, 50 cents down` 222.5 EQUALS 222
#ASSERT `rounded to the nearest dollar, 50 cents down` 222.51 EQUALS 223
#ASSERT `rounded to the nearest dollar, 50 cents down` 222.49 EQUALS 222

§§ `cl 11, 20(3), (4) -- malignant or non-malignant`

#ASSERT `Is my claim malignant or non-malignant` `meso` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a malignant claim`
#ASSERT `Is my claim malignant or non-malignant` `asbestosis` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a non-malignant claim`
#ASSERT `Is my claim malignant or non-malignant` `asbestosis` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `a non-malignant claim treated as a malignant claim`
#ASSERT `Is my claim malignant or non-malignant` `asbestosis` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `a non-malignant claim treated as a malignant claim`
#ASSERT `Is my claim malignant or non-malignant` `silicosis` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not a claim the claims resolution process applies to`
#ASSERT `Is my claim malignant or non-malignant` `no dust` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not a claim the claims resolution process applies to`

§§ `cl 13, 16, 20(1), 100(3)-(5) -- in the process`

-- Filed, nothing else has happened: in.
#ASSERT `Is my claim in the claims resolution process` `meso` `sufferer` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A relatives' claim through the deceased: in.
#ASSERT `Is my claim in the claims resolution process` `asbestosis` `through` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Silicosis: Part 3 applies only to asbestos-related claims.
#ASSERT `Is my claim in the claims resolution process` `silicosis` `sufferer` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Someone not claiming through the sufferer.
#ASSERT `Is my claim in the claims resolution process` `meso` `someone else` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not yet filed.
#ASSERT `Is my claim in the claims resolution process` `meso` `sufferer` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Pending before 1 September 2019: cl 100(4) ceased on 1 March 2020 (cl 100(5)), so Part 3 now extends to it (cl 100(3)).
#ASSERT `Is my claim in the claims resolution process` `meso` `sufferer` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same, with a 2013 Regulation mediation or apportionment still running (cl 100(5)): not answered.
#ASSERT `Is my claim in the claims resolution process` `meso` `sufferer` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A running 2013 process is irrelevant to a claim not pending before 1 September 2019.
#ASSERT `Is my claim in the claims resolution process` `meso` `sufferer` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Determined urgent; removed by agreement; removed for a failure.
#ASSERT `Is my claim in the claims resolution process` `meso` `sufferer` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my claim in the claims resolution process` `meso` `sufferer` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my claim in the claims resolution process` `meso` `sufferer` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Settled with an order; mediation concluded and cl 40 complied with; the same, with the parties' extension (cl 16(3)).
#ASSERT `Is my claim in the claims resolution process` `meso` `sufferer` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my claim in the claims resolution process` `meso` `sufferer` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my claim in the claims resolution process` `meso` `sufferer` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `cl 20(2), (3), (5) -- urgency`

#ASSERT `Is my claim urgent` `meso` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `determine the claim urgent: it leaves the claims resolution process (cl 20(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Is my claim urgent` `meso` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `determine the claim urgent: it leaves the claims resolution process (cl 20(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Is my claim urgent` `meso` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the claim is not urgent (cl 20(2): urgent only if)`
-- Non-malignant: no best efforts yet; satisfied but not urgent on the malignant timetable; urgent even so; not satisfied.
#ASSERT `Is my claim urgent` `asbestosis` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the application must not be made yet: the parties must first use their best efforts to agree to treat it as malignant (cl 20(5))`
#ASSERT `Is my claim urgent` `asbestosis` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `instead of determining it urgent, order that it be treated as a malignant claim (cl 20(3))`
#ASSERT `Is my claim urgent` `asbestosis` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `determine the claim urgent: it leaves the claims resolution process (cl 20(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Is my claim urgent` `asbestosis` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the claim is not urgent (cl 20(2): urgent only if)`
#ASSERT `Is my claim urgent` `silicosis` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not a claim the claims resolution process applies to`

§§ `The timetable, in business days`

-- Malignant, one defendant: cl 25(2) 10; cl 26(4) 20; cl 26(5) 30; cl 29(1) 10; cl 29(2) 20; cl 51(2) 35; cl 52(7) 40; cl 34(1) 30; cl 35(1) 45.
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `cross-claims filed and served (cl 25(2))` `meso` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `the reply of an original defendant (cl 26(4))` `meso` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 20
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `the reply of any other defendant or cross-defendant (cl 26(5))` `meso` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `notice that a defendant requires a medical examination (cl 29(1))` `meso` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `the medical examination (cl 29(2))` `meso` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 20
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `the defendants' agreement on apportionment (cl 51(2))` `meso` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 35
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `the Contributions Assessor's determination (cl 52(7))` `meso` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `referral for mediation (cl 34(1))` `meso` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `conclusion of mediation (cl 35(1))` `meso` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 45
-- Malignant, more than one defendant: cl 29(1) 20; cl 29(2) 30; cl 34(1) 50; cl 35(1) 60.
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `notice that a defendant requires a medical examination (cl 29(1))` `meso` FALSE TRUE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 20
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `the medical examination (cl 29(2))` `meso` FALSE TRUE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `referral for mediation (cl 34(1))` `meso` FALSE TRUE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 50
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `conclusion of mediation (cl 35(1))` `meso` FALSE TRUE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 60
-- Non-malignant, one and more than one defendant.
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `cross-claims filed and served (cl 25(2))` `asbestosis` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `the reply of an original defendant (cl 26(4))` `asbestosis` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `the reply of any other defendant or cross-defendant (cl 26(5))` `asbestosis` FALSE TRUE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 60
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `notice that a defendant requires a medical examination (cl 29(1))` `asbestosis` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `notice that a defendant requires a medical examination (cl 29(1))` `asbestosis` FALSE TRUE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 50
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `the medical examination (cl 29(2))` `asbestosis` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `the medical examination (cl 29(2))` `asbestosis` FALSE TRUE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 60
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `the defendants' agreement on apportionment (cl 51(2))` `asbestosis` FALSE TRUE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 70
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `the Contributions Assessor's determination (cl 52(7))` `asbestosis` FALSE TRUE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 80
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `referral for mediation (cl 34(1))` `asbestosis` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 60
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `referral for mediation (cl 34(1))` `asbestosis` FALSE TRUE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `conclusion of mediation (cl 35(1))` `asbestosis` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 90
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `conclusion of mediation (cl 35(1))` `asbestosis` FALSE TRUE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 120
-- A non-malignant claim treated as malignant runs on the malignant timetable.
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `conclusion of mediation (cl 35(1))` `asbestosis` TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 45
-- Extensions, malignant, more than one defendant: conclusion 60 + 3 suspended + 10 cross-claim + 5 registrar + 5 mediator + 2 x 1 revoked + 2 x 1 objection = 87.
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `conclusion of mediation (cl 35(1))` `meso` FALSE TRUE 3 10 5 5 1 1 EQUALS JUST 87
-- Referral 50 + 10 cross-claim + 2 x 2 objections = 64; the registrar deferral does not touch it.
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `referral for mediation (cl 34(1))` `meso` FALSE TRUE 0 10 5 0 0 2 EQUALS JUST 64
-- Assessor 40 + 10 + 2 = 52; agreement on apportionment 35 + 10 (no objection effect) = 45.
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `the Contributions Assessor's determination (cl 52(7))` `meso` FALSE TRUE 0 10 0 0 0 1 EQUALS JUST 52
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `the defendants' agreement on apportionment (cl 51(2))` `meso` FALSE TRUE 0 10 0 0 0 1 EQUALS JUST 45
-- A cross-claim extension extends the cross-claim period itself, not a period that ends with it (malignant, one
-- defendant: medical notice 10 = cross-claim 10), and not an original defendant's reply (fork F4); it does extend the
-- medical notice where there is more than one defendant (20 > 10).
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `cross-claims filed and served (cl 25(2))` `meso` FALSE FALSE 0 10 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 20
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `notice that a defendant requires a medical examination (cl 29(1))` `meso` FALSE FALSE 0 10 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `notice that a defendant requires a medical examination (cl 29(1))` `meso` FALSE TRUE 0 10 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `the reply of an original defendant (cl 26(4))` `meso` FALSE TRUE 0 10 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 20
-- Caps: cross-claim extension 10 / 20 in total; registrar deferral 5 / 20. At the cap, fine; one over, NOTHING.
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `cross-claims filed and served (cl 25(2))` `meso` FALSE FALSE 0 11 0 0 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `cross-claims filed and served (cl 25(2))` `asbestosis` FALSE FALSE 0 20 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 50
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `cross-claims filed and served (cl 25(2))` `asbestosis` FALSE FALSE 0 21 0 0 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `conclusion of mediation (cl 35(1))` `meso` FALSE FALSE 0 0 6 0 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `conclusion of mediation (cl 35(1))` `asbestosis` FALSE FALSE 0 0 20 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 110
-- Not a Part 3 claim.
#ASSERT `How many business days does this step have` `conclusion of mediation (cl 35(1))` `silicosis` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `The timetable, as dates`

-- Particulars on the last original defendant on Monday 1 February 2027. Business day n after it: 1-4 = 2-5 Feb, 5-9 =
-- 8-12 Feb, 10-14 = 15-19 Feb, 15-19 = 22-26 Feb, 20-24 = 1-5 Mar, 25-29 = 8-12 Mar, 30-34 = 15-19 Mar, 35-39 = 22-26
-- Mar, 40-44 = 29 Mar-2 Apr, 45-49 = 5-9 Apr, 50-54 = 12-16 Apr, 55-59 = 19-23 Apr, 60-64 = 26-30 Apr.
-- Malignant, one defendant: cross-claims day 10 = Monday 15 February.
#ASSERT `By when must this step be done` `cross-claims filed and served (cl 25(2))` `meso` FALSE FALSE `1 Feb 2027` `1 Feb 2027` FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST (`the regulation date` 15 2 2027)
-- Referral day 30 = Monday 15 March; conclusion day 45 = Monday 5 April.
#ASSERT `By when must this step be done` `referral for mediation (cl 34(1))` `meso` FALSE FALSE `1 Feb 2027` `1 Feb 2027` FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST (`the regulation date` 15 3 2027)
#ASSERT `By when must this step be done` `conclusion of mediation (cl 35(1))` `meso` FALSE FALSE `1 Feb 2027` `1 Feb 2027` FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST (`the regulation date` 5 4 2027)
-- With Good Friday (26 March) and Easter Monday (29 March 2027) in the period: day 47 = Wednesday 7 April.
#ASSERT `By when must this step be done` `conclusion of mediation (cl 35(1))` `meso` FALSE FALSE `1 Feb 2027` `1 Feb 2027` FALSE 2 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST (`the regulation date` 7 4 2027)
-- More than one defendant: conclusion day 60 = Monday 26 April; the Assessor day 40 = Monday 29 March; agreement day 35 = Monday 22 March; medical notice day 20 = Monday 1 March.
#ASSERT `By when must this step be done` `conclusion of mediation (cl 35(1))` `meso` FALSE TRUE `1 Feb 2027` `1 Feb 2027` FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST (`the regulation date` 26 4 2027)
#ASSERT `By when must this step be done` `the Contributions Assessor's determination (cl 52(7))` `meso` FALSE TRUE `1 Feb 2027` `1 Feb 2027` FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST (`the regulation date` 29 3 2027)
#ASSERT `By when must this step be done` `the defendants' agreement on apportionment (cl 51(2))` `meso` FALSE TRUE `1 Feb 2027` `1 Feb 2027` FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST (`the regulation date` 22 3 2027)
#ASSERT `By when must this step be done` `notice that a defendant requires a medical examination (cl 29(1))` `meso` FALSE TRUE `1 Feb 2027` `1 Feb 2027` FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST (`the regulation date` 1 3 2027)
-- An original defendant's reply counts from service of the claim on it: claim served Friday 5 February, day 20 = Friday 5 March (8-12 Feb 1-5, 15-19 6-10, 22-26 11-15, 1-5 Mar 16-20).
#ASSERT `By when must this step be done` `the reply of an original defendant (cl 26(4))` `meso` FALSE FALSE `1 Feb 2027` (`the regulation date` 5 2 2027) FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST (`the regulation date` 5 3 2027)
-- Non-malignant cross-claims: day 30 = Monday 15 March.
#ASSERT `By when must this step be done` `cross-claims filed and served (cl 25(2))` `asbestosis` FALSE FALSE `1 Feb 2027` `1 Feb 2027` FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST (`the regulation date` 15 3 2027)
-- Across Christmas: particulars served Tuesday 22 December 2026, malignant cross-claims (10): Wed 23 (1), Thu 24 (2), then from Monday 11 January: 11 (3), 12 (4), 13 (5), 14 (6), 15 (7), 18 (8), 19 (9), 20 (10) = Wednesday 20 January 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must this step be done` `cross-claims filed and served (cl 25(2))` `meso` FALSE FALSE (`the regulation date` 22 12 2026) `1 Feb 2027` FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST (`the regulation date` 20 1 2027)
-- The parties agreed to count the Christmas period; Christmas Day, the Boxing Day holiday (28 December) and New Year's Day are 3 weekday public holidays: 13 counted weekdays: 23, 24, 25, 28, 29, 30, 31 Dec, 1, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8 Jan = Friday 8 January 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must this step be done` `cross-claims filed and served (cl 25(2))` `meso` FALSE FALSE (`the regulation date` 22 12 2026) `1 Feb 2027` TRUE 3 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST (`the regulation date` 8 1 2027)
#ASSERT `By when must this step be done` `cross-claims filed and served (cl 25(2))` `silicosis` FALSE FALSE `1 Feb 2027` `1 Feb 2027` FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `cl 16(6), 23(5), 34(2) -- notices to the registrar`

-- Particulars on the last original defendant Friday 5 February 2027; 5 business days: 8, 9, 10, 11, 12 February.
#ASSERT `Is my notice to the registrar in time` `the date my statement of particulars was served on the last original defendant (cl 23(5))` (`the regulation date` 5 2 2027) (`the regulation date` 12 2 2027) FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my notice to the registrar in time` `the date my statement of particulars was served on the last original defendant (cl 23(5))` (`the regulation date` 5 2 2027) (`the regulation date` 15 2 2027) FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- With one weekday public holiday in the period, Monday 15 February is the 5th business day.
#ASSERT `Is my notice to the registrar in time` `the date my statement of particulars was served on the last original defendant (cl 23(5))` (`the regulation date` 5 2 2027) (`the regulation date` 15 2 2027) FALSE FALSE 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Referred for mediation Friday 5 March: Monday 8 March is in time, Tuesday 9 March is not; the same day is in time.
#ASSERT `Is my notice to the registrar in time` `the claim being referred for mediation (cl 34(2)(a))` (`the regulation date` 5 3 2027) (`the regulation date` 8 3 2027) FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my notice to the registrar in time` `the claim being referred for mediation (cl 34(2)(a))` (`the regulation date` 5 3 2027) (`the regulation date` 9 3 2027) FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my notice to the registrar in time` `the claim being referred for mediation (cl 34(2)(a))` (`the regulation date` 5 3 2027) (`the regulation date` 5 3 2027) FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Settled, with an application for consent judgment filed: no notice needed (fork F6); without one, the 1-day limit.
#ASSERT `Is my notice to the registrar in time` `the claim being settled (cl 34(2)(b))` (`the regulation date` 5 3 2027) (`the regulation date` 12 3 2027) TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is my notice to the registrar in time` `the claim being settled (cl 34(2)(b))` (`the regulation date` 5 3 2027) (`the regulation date` 12 3 2027) FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An agreement to suspend made Wednesday 23 December 2026: Thu 24 (1), then 11 (2), 12 (3), 13 (4), 14 (5) January; Friday 15 January is late.
#ASSERT `Is my notice to the registrar in time` `an agreement to extend or suspend the claims resolution process (cl 16(6))` (`the regulation date` 23 12 2026) (`the regulation date` 14 1 2027) FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my notice to the registrar in time` `an agreement to extend or suspend the claims resolution process (cl 16(6))` (`the regulation date` 23 12 2026) (`the regulation date` 15 1 2027) FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `cl 26(8), 28 -- further information`

-- Mediation starts Monday 15 March 2027; 5 business days before: Fri 12 (1), Thu 11 (2), Wed 10 (3), Tue 9 (4), Mon 8 March (5).
#ASSERT `Have I given the further information in time` TRUE `1 Feb 2027` (`the regulation date` 15 3 2027) (`the regulation date` 8 3 2027) FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Have I given the further information in time` TRUE `1 Feb 2027` (`the regulation date` 15 3 2027) (`the regulation date` 9 3 2027) FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- With one weekday public holiday in those days, the latest day moves to Friday 5 March; Monday 8 March is then late.
#ASSERT `Have I given the further information in time` TRUE `1 Feb 2027` (`the regulation date` 15 3 2027) (`the regulation date` 8 3 2027) FALSE 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An unreasonable requirement: cl 26(8) does not reach it.
#ASSERT `Have I given the further information in time` FALSE `1 Feb 2027` (`the regulation date` 15 3 2027) (`the regulation date` 8 3 2027) FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Required on Tuesday 9 March, after the latest day (fork F7).
#ASSERT `Have I given the further information in time` TRUE (`the regulation date` 9 3 2027) (`the regulation date` 15 3 2027) (`the regulation date` 9 3 2027) FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `By when must the defendant answer my request` (`the regulation date` 15 3 2027) FALSE 0 EQUALS `the regulation date` 8 3 2027
#ASSERT `By when must the defendant answer my request` (`the regulation date` 15 3 2027) FALSE 1 EQUALS `the regulation date` 5 3 2027

§§ `cl 29 -- medical examinations`

-- Malignant, more than one defendant: notice by day 20 (Monday 1 March), examination by day 30 (Monday 15 March).
#ASSERT `Is the medical examination requirement in time` `meso` FALSE TRUE TRUE `1 Feb 2027` (`the regulation date` 1 3 2027) (`the regulation date` 15 3 2027) FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the medical examination requirement in time` `meso` FALSE TRUE TRUE `1 Feb 2027` (`the regulation date` 1 3 2027) (`the regulation date` 16 3 2027) FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the medical examination requirement in time` `meso` FALSE TRUE TRUE `1 Feb 2027` (`the regulation date` 2 3 2027) (`the regulation date` 15 3 2027) FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The parties varied the examination period: a late examination is no breach of cl 29(2); the notice limit still applies.
#ASSERT `Is the medical examination requirement in time` `meso` FALSE TRUE TRUE `1 Feb 2027` (`the regulation date` 1 3 2027) (`the regulation date` 30 4 2027) TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A 10-day cross-claim extension extends both periods (30 and 40): notice Monday 15 March, examination Monday 29 March.
#ASSERT `Is the medical examination requirement in time` `meso` FALSE TRUE TRUE `1 Feb 2027` (`the regulation date` 15 3 2027) (`the regulation date` 29 3 2027) FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 10 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Served Monday 15 February: notice by day 20 (Monday 15 March); the examination period's day 30 is Monday 29 March, and
-- Good Friday (26 March) and Easter Monday (29 March) 2027 move it to Wednesday 31 March. The Easter holidays fall after
-- the notice limit, so they do not extend it: notice on Tuesday 16 March is a day late.
#ASSERT `Is the medical examination requirement in time` `meso` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`the regulation date` 15 2 2027) (`the regulation date` 15 3 2027) (`the regulation date` 31 3 2027) FALSE FALSE 0 2 0 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the medical examination requirement in time` `meso` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`the regulation date` 15 2 2027) (`the regulation date` 16 3 2027) (`the regulation date` 29 3 2027) FALSE FALSE 0 2 0 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the medical examination requirement in time` `meso` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`the regulation date` 15 2 2027) (`the regulation date` 15 3 2027) (`the regulation date` 1 4 2027) FALSE FALSE 0 2 0 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Malignant, one defendant: notice by day 10 (Monday 15 February), examination by day 20 (Monday 1 March).
#ASSERT `Is the medical examination requirement in time` `meso` FALSE FALSE TRUE `1 Feb 2027` (`the regulation date` 15 2 2027) (`the regulation date` 1 3 2027) FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the medical examination requirement in time` `meso` FALSE FALSE TRUE `1 Feb 2027` (`the regulation date` 16 2 2027) (`the regulation date` 1 3 2027) FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A cross-defendant (fork F8); a silicosis claim.
#ASSERT `Is the medical examination requirement in time` `meso` FALSE TRUE FALSE `1 Feb 2027` (`the regulation date` 1 3 2027) (`the regulation date` 15 3 2027) FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is the medical examination requirement in time` `silicosis` FALSE TRUE TRUE `1 Feb 2027` (`the regulation date` 1 3 2027) (`the regulation date` 15 3 2027) FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I choose a joint medical examination` 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I choose a joint medical examination` 3 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I choose a joint medical examination` 1 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `cl 25 -- cross-claims`

-- Malignant: 5 already + 5 asked = 10, the cap; no prejudice shown: taken to consent; prejudice shown: may refuse.
#ASSERT `Can I refuse more time for cross-claims` `meso` FALSE TRUE 5 5 FALSE EQUALS `you are taken to consent: you cannot show the extension would substantially prejudice you (cl 25(5))`
#ASSERT `Can I refuse more time for cross-claims` `meso` FALSE TRUE 5 5 TRUE EQUALS `you may refuse: you can show the extension would substantially prejudice you (cl 25(5))`
#ASSERT `Can I refuse more time for cross-claims` `meso` FALSE TRUE 5 6 FALSE EQUALS `the extension cannot be given: the total would exceed the cap (cl 25(4))`
#ASSERT `Can I refuse more time for cross-claims` `asbestosis` FALSE TRUE 0 20 FALSE EQUALS `you are taken to consent: you cannot show the extension would substantially prejudice you (cl 25(5))`
#ASSERT `Can I refuse more time for cross-claims` `asbestosis` FALSE TRUE 0 21 FALSE EQUALS `the extension cannot be given: the total would exceed the cap (cl 25(4))`
-- Treated as malignant: the cap is 10.
#ASSERT `Can I refuse more time for cross-claims` `asbestosis` TRUE TRUE 0 11 FALSE EQUALS `the extension cannot be given: the total would exceed the cap (cl 25(4))`
#ASSERT `Can I refuse more time for cross-claims` `meso` FALSE FALSE 0 5 FALSE EQUALS `the request came too late: it can only be made before the period ends (cl 25(3))`
#ASSERT `Can I refuse more time for cross-claims` `silicosis` FALSE TRUE 0 5 FALSE EQUALS `not a claim the claims resolution process applies to`
#ASSERT `May I refuse consent to joining the insurer` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May I refuse consent to joining the insurer` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I refuse consent to joining the insurer` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

